 <section class="resources" aria-label="Your resources across life"><div class="section-line"><h2>Your life, so far</h2><span>Game values · not predictions</span></div><p id="mood-note"></p><details class="comparison-note"><summary>About the comparison</summary><p class="fine">Comparison: alternate paths from the same starting conditions. This is not a population average.</p><p id="cohort-note" class="fine"></p><p class="fine">Alternate paths keep cash and do not trade funds.</p><p class="fine">World colours follow recent changes; the recorded values do not change.</p></details><div class="graphs"><figure><figcaption><span>Physical health</span><strong id="health-value">90 / 100</strong><small id="health-reference" class="reference"></small></figcaption><svg id="health-chart" viewBox="0 0 360 114" role="img" aria-label="Physical health over age"></svg></figure><figure><figcaption><span>Wellbeing</span><strong id="wellbeing-value">65 / 100</strong><small id="wellbeing-reference" class="reference"></small></figcaption><svg id="wellbeing-chart" viewBox="0 0 360 114" role="img" aria-label="Wellbeing over age"></svg></figure><figure><figcaption><span id="cash-label">Household buffer</span><strong id="cash-value">฿18,000</strong><small id="cash-reference" class="reference"></small></figcaption><svg id="cash-chart" viewBox="0 0 360 114" role="img" aria-label="Household cash buffer over age"></svg></figure></div><details id="family-history" class="family-history" hidden><summary>Household buffer history</summary><svg id="family-cash-chart" viewBox="0 0 360 114" role="img" aria-label="Household cash buffer over age"></svg></details><ul class="event-list" id="event-list" aria-label="Events"></ul><p id="event-detail" aria-live="polite">Select a marker to read the event.</p><details id="self-record"><summary>Body, mind &amp; personality</summary><p id="starting-record" class="fine"></p><p class="fine">Game indices, not psychological tests. Big Five traits are separate from reasoning and emotional skills.</p><div id="capacities"></div><h3>Your dispositions</h3><p class="fine">Thin marks show your starting record. Filled bars show the current model.</p><div id="traits"></div><p class="fine">Traits suggest challenges, not career bans. Wellbeing is not a dopamine measurement.</p></details></section>
 <details class="method"><summary>Rules, sources &amp; what this prototype leaves out</summary><div><p>This prototype uses authored game rules. Its money, health changes and event odds are not measured population statistics.</p><p>The graphs join five-year snapshots. Markers sit at the recorded review age, not an exact event date.</p><p>Ten points are a game constraint. Reasoning, empathy and strength are not biological opposites.</p><p>Smoking has costs in this model, without guaranteed happiness. Beliefs have no universal morality score.</p><p>The neighbourhood is metaphorical. Nearby buildings represent parts of a life, not a real map.</p><p>Marriage and family milestones follow your choices. Dengue, job loss and pregnancy are not yet generated by this model.</p><p><a href="../start/#research">Research</a> · <a href="https://www.who.int/news-room/fact-sheets/detail/dengue-and-severe-dengue">WHO: Dengue</a> · <a href="https://www.who.int/news-room/fact-sheets/detail/hiv-aids">WHO: HIV and AIDS</a></p></div></details></main></body></html>
